## maistro-engine — universal agent rules

- Start with `AGENTS.md` and `docs/agent-guidance/README.md`. Use progressive disclosure: load only the domain index and atomic guidance applicable to the current task; do not preload the ADR/spec corpus.
- Prefer implementing and changing code under `packages/*/src/`, especially `packages/maistro-core/src/maistro/`. Do not add product code at repo root `src/` (see `AGENTS.md`).
- Run `uv run pytest` after non-trivial Python changes; scope tests to affected packages when possible.
- Use `uv run ruff check` / `ruff format` on touched files; respect existing types (mypy strict).
- Never commit secrets or `.env` files. Use environment variables and document required vars in PRs or ADRs. Never hand-edit `.cursor/rules/imported/`.
- Read relevant ADRs in `docs/adr/` before changing cross-product contracts or public APIs (discover via `docs/agent-guidance/`).
- Surface conflicting guidance instead of silently preserving historical behavior; pre-1.0 work follows the intended 1.0 architecture and canonical atomic standards.
